  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>A face-centered cubic (fcc) unit cell contains a component in the center of each face in addition to those at the corners of the cube. The atoms touch each other along the face diagonal.</p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>FCC</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math></p><p>A body-centered cubic (bcc) unit cell contains a component in the center of the cube&nbsp;in addition to those at the corners of the cube.&nbsp;The atoms touch each other along the body&nbsp;diagonal.<br /><br />For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BCC</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
